.TH INTEGRATION-TEST-TOOL 1 "2026-09-06" "gettoken" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
integration-test-tool \- stand in for an integrated tool so the chain can be verified
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B integration-test-tool
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B integration-test-tool
is the tool the verification suite integrates. It exists so the whole chain can
be exercised without reaching a real service.
.PP
It reads
.B INTEGRATIONTEST_TOKEN
from the environment and runs only when that variable holds the token the
.I integrationtest/ci/run
capability downgrades to. It refuses the super\-token that token was traded
for, so a run that succeeds is proof that a downgrade happened.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B INTEGRATIONTEST_TOKEN
The access token to run on.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The token allowed
.IR integrationtest/ci/run .
.TP
.B 1
It did not. The reason is on standard error.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR gettoken (1)
